    ontouml:description "\"Each Form is its essence (ousia), which is to say that the relation of Being links the essence of beauty to the subject, Beauty itself. Being, then, is a primitive ontological relation designed exclusively to capture the special tie between that which possesses an essence and the essence possessed.\"  (Silverman)" ;
